<article class="env-lemma" id="0EFE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EFE">Lemma <span data-tag="0EFE">51.10.2</span>.</a> Let $I$ be an ideal of a Noetherian ring $A$. Let $M$ be a finite $A$-module, let $\mathfrak p \subset A$ be a prime ideal, and let $s \geq 0$ be an integer. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$A$ has a dualizing complex, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathfrak p \not\in V(I)$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for all primes $\mathfrak p' \subset \mathfrak p$ and $\mathfrak q \in V(I)$ with $\mathfrak p' \subset \mathfrak q$ we have 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \text{depth}_{A_{\mathfrak p'}}(M_{\mathfrak p'}) + \dim ((A/\mathfrak p')_\mathfrak q) > s  \]
</div>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then there exists an $f \in A$, $f \not\in \mathfrak p$ which annihilates $H^ i_{V(I)}(M)$ for $i \leq s$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Consider the sets 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  T = V(I) \quad \text{and}\quad T' = \bigcup \nolimits _{f \in A, f \not\in \mathfrak p} V(f)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       These are subsets of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ stable under specialization. Observe that $T \subset T'$ and $\mathfrak p \not\in T'$. Assumption (3) says that hypothesis (2) of Proposition <a href="/tag/0EFC" data-tag="0EFC">51.10.1</a> holds. Hence we can find $J \subset A$ with $V(J) \subset T'$ such that $J H^ i_{V(I)}(M) = 0$ for $i \leq s$. Choose $f \in A$, $f \not\in \mathfrak p$ with $V(J) \subset V(f)$. A power of $f$ annihilates $H^ i_{V(I)}(M)$ for $i \leq s$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>